    "teach_4": {
      "id": "teach_4",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Adding pure concentrate can raise a percentage.\n\nA 20 L solution is 30% acid → 6 L acid.\nAdd x L pure acid.\n\nTo become 50% acid:\n(6+x)/(20+x)=1/2.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_4_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_4_step": {
      "id": "teach_4_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "2(6+x)=20+x\n12+2x=20+x\nx=8 L.\n\nBoth the acid amount and the total volume increase by x. That is why the variable appears in numerator and denominator.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_4"
        }
      ]
    },
